---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/compare/sequenzy-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = 'Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS: Shopify Migration in 2026';
const desc = 'Replacing retired Yotpo Email and SMS with Sequenzy or another sender: preserve Reviews and Loyalty, reconcile permissions, and verify event handoffs.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Sequenzy or Yotpo Email better for a Shopify store already on Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Yotpo retired Email and SMS; this is now a replacement decision. Keeping Yotpo Reviews does not require keeping the retired sender. Evaluate Sequenzy for the email journeys you need and confirm how review status reaches it before promising review-based branches."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare migration costs at 20,000 contacts?",
    "answer": "Contact count alone is insufficient. Model planned email volume, SMS destinations and segments, retained Reviews and Loyalty contracts, and integration work. Sequenzy advertises email-volume billing with unlimited contacts. An old Yotpo messaging invoice is historical spending, not a current replacement quote."
  },
  {
    "question": "What happens to review and UGC integration?",
    "answer": "Yotpo still offers Reviews and Loyalty. Preserve review collection and storefront display independently of replacing email. Check the destination connector for review-request ownership, reviewer status and permitted content access; this comparison does not establish a native Yotpo-to-Sequenzy connector."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I use Sequenzy for email and Yotpo for reviews only?",
    "answer": "That is a proposed architecture to validate, not a tested configuration here. Assign review requests to one owner and verify identity matching, permissions and field freshness before using Yotpo data in Sequenzy. Shopify order sync alone does not prove review-status sync."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Sequenzy replace Yotpo SMS?",
    "answer": "Do not assume full replacement. Sequenzy lists a paid SMS/MMS beta using a US/Canada toll-free number. Validate destination countries, sender setup, consent import and required workflows separately. The retired Yotpo SMS service is not a continuing fallback."
  },
  {
    "question": "How do I restore loyalty-triggered email?",
    "answer": "Keep Yotpo as the loyalty record if retaining that product. Map tier changes, balances and reward redemption to the new sender through a verified integration. A historical tier tag is not proof that a reward remains available when a delayed message sends."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I handle Black Friday after migration?",
    "answer": "Start with a reconciled audience and working unsubscribe paths. Check current reward eligibility and inventory before scheduling VIP campaigns. Rebuild seasonal messages in the destination rather than replaying an old queue; compare actual previews and logs before expanding volume."
  },
  {
    "question": "What workflow test should decide the replacement?",
    "answer": "Use test identities to follow an order through review request, review submission, loyalty change and redemption. Confirm that the destination sends only the intended message, suppresses revoked permission and handles repeated or late events. Choose based on the demonstrated workflow and ongoing ownership, not an assumed winner."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a><span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span><span>Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email &amp; SMS</span></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Retirement and replacement</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email &amp; SMS for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">In 2026 this is a migration decision. Separate the retired messaging service from the Reviews and Loyalty products you may retain, then evaluate whether Sequenzy can receive the data and permissions your replacement journeys require.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Yotpo messaging is retired; Reviews and Loyalty continue</h2>
        <p>Yotpo's <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">September 2025 migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025 and named Attentive and Omnisend as migration partners. The <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current SMS notice</a> says its dashboard and background services are no longer active. Do not plan a trial against a live Yotpo messaging account or assume old exports remain accessible.</p>
        <p>Yotpo's <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/pricing/">current product catalog</a> still offers Reviews &amp; UGC and Loyalty &amp; Referrals. Retaining them can preserve an existing review and rewards program while changing the sender. It does not restore the retired email or SMS service. Review collection, points accounting and promotional delivery need separate owners.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits the replacement decision</h2>
        <p>Sequenzy's <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/shopify-integration">Shopify integration page</a> advertises customer, order and product sync, purchase-based segments and order-event automations. Those are useful building blocks for post-purchase email. They do not establish that Yotpo review submissions, point balances or tier changes arrive automatically.</p>
        <p>Its <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">current feature and pricing page</a> lists visual workflows, assisted drafts and email-volume billing with unlimited contacts. It also lists a paid SMS/MMS beta using a US/Canada toll-free number. Assess email and SMS separately: beta scope and sender geography may not match a former Yotpo program. Supplier feature descriptions are not evidence of a completed migration or improved revenue.</p>
        <p>Sequenzy is worth evaluating when Shopify-driven email and editable workflows cover your requirements. If your operation depends on an established Yotpo partner handoff, include Yotpo's named partners in the shortlist and examine their current connector scope. A partner recommendation from 2025 is not proof of today's account terms or a guarantee that every historical workflow transfers.</p>
        <h2>Inventory what survives before rebuilding flows</h2>
        <p>Start from available exports, Shopify records, existing integration logs and retained Yotpo products. Mark unavailable history as missing rather than reconstructing it as fact. Capture templates, audience definitions, offer expiries and the last known sender for each workflow. Rebuilding a welcome sequence does not mean everyone in the old database should receive it again.</p>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Record or job</th><th>Proposed owner</th><th>Acceptance check</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Orders and fulfillment</td><td>Shopify; destination receives events</td><td>Stable order ID, event time, refund and cancellation handling</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Review collection and display</td><td>Retained Yotpo Reviews</td><td>One request owner; completed review does not trigger another ask</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Points and reward eligibility</td><td>Retained Yotpo Loyalty</td><td>Current balance and redemption state available before a reward message</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Email and SMS delivery</td><td>Chosen destination for each channel</td><td>Current permission, sender readiness and suppression at send time</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Migration reconciliation</td><td>Named store operator</td><td>Counts, exceptions and missing evidence recorded before activation</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h2>Keep permission separate from customer identity</h2>
        <p>A Shopify customer ID helps join orders to a person; it is not marketing permission. Preserve the available channel-specific subscription state, source, timestamp and suppression history. An email opt-in must not become an SMS opt-in during import. Treat records with missing or conflicting evidence as exceptions for review before activation rather than silently making them subscribed.</p>
        <p>Reconcile old exports against later changes wherever those records are available. A fresh unsubscribe must not be overwritten by an older subscribed row. Confirm destination import semantics on test records first: does importing a customer activate automations, reset a subscription or replace a suppression? Keep the destination paused until those effects are understood.</p>
        <h2>A proposed review-to-reward journey</h2>
        <p>Consider a homewares shop retaining Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty while rebuilding email in Sequenzy. This is a proposed test, not a merchant result. Shopify fulfillment starts product-care email in the destination. Yotpo owns the review request. A review submission updates reviewer status; a separate loyalty event may award points according to the store's program. Neither event should be treated as new promotional permission.</p>
        <p>Map customer ID, order ID, review ID, event ID, occurrence time and receipt time. A connector or custom handoff must demonstrate those fields; no direct Sequenzy–Yotpo connector is established here. If the required data cannot be delivered reliably, keep that message with a supported integration or simplify the journey rather than claiming a tag provides full parity.</p>
        <p>Now redeem the reward before a delayed points reminder becomes due. The message should recheck eligibility or exit; a stale balance must not promise a spent reward. Submit the same review event twice and deliver an older tier event after a newer one. Record whether the integration deduplicates the event and preserves the current tier. These checks distinguish a functioning handoff from a successful CSV upload.</p>
        <h2>Rebuild eligible work, not the retired queue</h2>
        <p>A late cart event, an already-fulfilled order and an expired loyalty offer require different treatment. Define which event ages remain useful for each journey, using the actual offer and fulfillment policy. Do not apply an arbitrary shared delay to all messages. Exclude completed purchases from recovery and prevent historical imports from restarting welcome flows.</p>
        <p>Before switching on delivery, identify every remaining sender: Shopify notifications, review requests, loyalty messages, the replacement ESP and any SMS provider. The retired service cannot be your rollback plan. A safe rollback pauses destination marketing while keeping essential order communication with its established owner. Reconcile uncertain sends before retrying them.</p>
        <h2>Model replacement costs and report a new baseline</h2>
        <p>Compare the destination's current quote with the work you will actually run: email volume, SMS destination and message segments, retained Yotpo contracts, connector charges and maintenance. Do not price Reviews and Loyalty as if they were replaced by email software. Include migration labor and any overlap separately from steady monthly spending.</p>
        <p>Hypothetical email planning example: four campaigns to 6,000 eligible recipients produce 24,000 sends. Another 2,000 customers receiving two post-purchase emails add 4,000, giving 28,000 planned emails. This is workload arithmetic, not a quote or revenue forecast. Count actual suppressions and other sends when choosing a plan; model SMS credits independently.</p>
        <p>Keep historical reports with their attribution definitions. A replacement may count orders or attribution windows differently, so a change in reported email revenue is not automatically a change in sales. Start a new baseline with intended audience, delivered messages, unsubscribes, complaints, orders and integration exceptions. Review-request completion and loyalty redemption belong in their own measures.</p>
        <h2>Make the migration decision on demonstrated ownership</h2>
        <p>Proceed with Sequenzy only when the email journey, permission behavior and any required Yotpo data handoff have been demonstrated in your setup. Select SMS on its own country, sender and workflow requirements. Keeping Reviews and Loyalty can be sensible when those products still serve the store; it is not a reason to describe Yotpo Email and SMS as an available suite.</p>
        <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">selection framework</a> to record unmet requirements and the <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">pricing guide</a> to separate recurring costs from migration work. This page documents supplier scope and proposed checks, not firsthand testing or a platform winner. Sources checked November 24, 2026.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/supplements">Email tools for supplement stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
